      <p>Chief executives, trustees and finance leads of UK charities preparing a trustees' annual report under the Charities SORP 2026. You may have plenty of activity to report and little evidence of change, or good evidence that never makes it into the report.</p>
      <h2>Why it matters now</h2>
      <p>The SORP 2026 applies to reporting periods beginning on or after 1 January 2026, so for most charities that means the year ending 31 December 2026 or 31 March 2027. Funders, examiners and the public will read the report for outcomes. A list of activities will no longer be enough, and drafting the section at the last minute rarely works.</p>
